torname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [a,b],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $y=f(x)=4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in [-2,2].$ \n\nSo, the parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\nr(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\,(4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,(4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [-2,2],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the second component of $r$ is $(4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac4af78-af9b-5d48-a5d7-7d47ad92e348" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Parametrization of a Surface of Revolution: Rotation About the x-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d97d1d5-911f-5e8d-8219-43eba48f80ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨x,\\,2\\pi (1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,2\\pi (1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373506} {:answer/id #uuid "eee3747c-6c2e-5f20-8ff4-f7fd97b7d591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨(1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,(1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,x⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373507} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa691bd-e0a1-545f-9678-4ae9298aaf9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\pi (1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,2\\pi (1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,x⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373508} {:answer/id #uuid "43db7c6e-52c6-56ee-bcdb-d939efd0b78a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨x,\\,(1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,(1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373509} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3dc743-df23-541a-a95b-bdd0cbfab30f" :answer/type {:db/ident :ans